Feature: TC_07_ENTS - Transfer Application E2E Regression Pack (Agent to ETF Partner)

  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Purpose:
  #   Single end-to-end regression journey covering Transfer of Entitlements flows where the Transferor is an Agent
  #   (aga6322) and the Transferee is a herd managed by an ETF Partner login.
  #
  #   Difference from Agent-to-Agent (TC_03 / TC_04) and Agent-to-Individual (TC_05 / TC_06):
  #     - the ETF partner accepts from the ETF button ("Access an application using Transfer Key") on the partner
  #       dashboard; when that button is not shown the standard View Transfer Application route is taken
  #     - the partner searches the transferee herd in Transfer Out first, like an agent
  #
  #   Transfer types covered:
  #     Section 1 : Change of Registration (205)  - Selenium: J1390696 to J1314060 (Teresa Noone)         partner aga6322
  #     Section 2 : Inheritance            (201)  - Selenium: J1400039 to J1350023 (Frehill Suppliers)    partner aga6322
  #     Section 3 : Gift                   (202)  - Selenium: JFP10136 to J199406X (Buckley Suppliers)    partner aga6454
  #     Section 4 : Lease                  (211)  - Selenium: J1400195 to J1970609 (David Vaughan)        partner aga6454 + lease year
  #     Section 5 : Merger                 (203)  - Selenium: J1400217 to J1930160 (Edward Grimes)        partner aga6066
  #     Section 6 : Division               (204)  - Selenium: J140033X to V2631112 (Nora White)           partner aga6322
  #     Section 7 : Sale                   (212)  - Selenium: JFP10136 to J1930305 (Michael Owen Galvin)  partner aga6066
  #     Section 8 : Change of Legal Entity (206)  - Selenium: J1350350 to A1030887 (John Joseph Mcgovern) partner aga6505
  #
  # Migrated from: TC_07_ENTS.feature (legacy 8 separate scenarios)
  #   TC_25 -> Section 1   TC_26 -> Section 2   TC_28 -> Section 3   TC_29 -> Section 4
  #   TC_30 -> Section 5   TC_31 -> Section 6   TC_32 -> Section 7   TC_33 -> Section 8
  #
  # Runtime data (Playwright, 30-09-2026):
  #   No herd or name is typed in this file. The ETF partner named in the transfereeAgent row manages the transferee
  #   herd, so each section is a cross-agent pick (EntsTestData.nextCrossAgentPair): the transferor herd comes from
  #   aga6322's Agent Login pool and the transferee herd from the partner's pool. When the partner is aga6322 itself
  #   (Sections 1, 2 and 6, as in the Selenium file) it is a same-agent pick.
  #     {transferor.herd}  {transferee.herd}  {transferee.name}  {transferee.agent}
  #   The ETF login step uses {transferee.agent}, so it always logs in as the partner named in the create table.
  #   The Selenium Section 4 transferor herd was pinned to agent aga6365; here every transferor comes from aga6322.
  #   Every pick is written to runtime-data/ents_used_herds.csv and never reused. Put a herd number, name or login back
  #   in any cell to pin it for debugging (the Selenium values are in the comments of each section).
  #
  # Step reuse:
  #   Background login / navigation        -> stepdefinitions.TC_03
  #   Login as a named user                -> stepdefinitions.ENTS.TC_08_ENTS
  #   Tab switching                        -> stepdefinitions.TC_06
  #   Create / upload / send / key / submit -> stepdefinitions.ENTS.TC_01_ENTS
  #   Transferor re-login between sections -> stepdefinitions.ENTS.TC_03_ENTS (the no-logout variant, as in Selenium)
  #   ETF partner login + acceptance       -> stepdefinitions.ENTS.TC_07_ENTS
  #
  # Author : Aniket Pathare | aniket.pathare@government.ie
  # Created: 31-03-2026 | Updated: 30-09-2026 (Playwright + runtime ENTS data)
  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Background:
    Given the agent user is on the login page
    When the individual logs in as transferor "aga6322"
    And the agent opens the "Basic Income Support for Sustainability" application
    Then the agent should land on the BISS Home page
    And the agent navigates to the "Home" and "My Clients" Left Menu Link
    And the agent switches to the "Transfers" tab on the My Client page

  @regression @transfers @agent-to-etf @e2e
  Scenario: AT-ENTS-TRANSFERS-E2E-07 - Agent completes all Agent-to-ETF Partner transfer types

    # ===========================================
    # SECTION 1 : Change of Registration (205)
    # Covers: TC_25
    # ETF Partner: aga6322 | Selenium: J1390696 to J1314060 (Teresa Noone)
    # ===========================================

    # --- Transferor (Agent aga6322) ---
    When the agent creates a transfer application with the following details
      | transferorHerd  | {transferor.herd}              |
      | transfereeHerd  | {transferee.herd}              |
      | transfereeName  | {transferee.name}              |
      | transfereeAgent | aga6322                        |
      | transferType    | Change of Registration Details |
      | entitlements    | 0.01                           |
      | notes           | Test Notes                     |
    And the agent uploads the transferor signature document
    And the agent sends the transfer for acceptance
    Then the transfer key should be captured

    # --- Transferee (ETF Partner) ---
    When the agent logs out and re-logs in as the ETF partner "{transferee.agent}"
    And the agent navigates to the "Home" and "My Clients" Left Menu Link
    And the agent switches to the "Transfers" tab on the My Client page
    And the ETF partner completes the transferee acceptance flow
      | transfereeHerd | {transferee.herd} |
      | notes          | Approved Test     |
    Then the transfer should be submitted successfully

